The bits is a list of 1, 0, 1, 0, and 1.
The last is the last position of bits.
The size is last plus 1.
The ones is an empty list of whole numbers.
For every spot from 0 to last.
If item spot of bits is 1, Place spot into ones.

The count is the number of items in ones.
The valid is 1.
If count is 0.
Show 0.
Show last.
Set valid to 0.

If count is more than 0 and count modulo 3 is not 0.
Show -1.
Show -1.
Set valid to 0.

The good is 1.
The left is -1.
The right is -1.
If valid is 1.
The group is count divided by 3.
The firststart is item 0 of ones.
The secondstart is item group of ones.
The thirdstart is item (group plus group) of ones.
The span is size minus thirdstart.
Set left to firststart plus span minus 1.
Set right to secondstart plus span.
For every offset from 0 to span minus 1.
The first is item (firststart plus offset) of bits.
The second is item (secondstart plus offset) of bits.
The third is item (thirdstart plus offset) of bits.
If first is not second, set good to 0.
If first is not third, set good to 0.

If valid is 1 and good is 0, show -1, show -1.
If valid is 1 and good is 1, Show left, Show right.
